            "summary": "RE-SPELLED AND SUBSTRATE BUILT; THE OBLIGATION DID NOT SHRINK (pic-c, 0092 r6). Released, unowned. Five files, rooted, 0 sorries, all declarations axiom-clean [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound] vs a control firing sorryAx; lake build 8888 jobs EXIT=0.\n\nTHE HEADLINE, WITH ITS OWN CORRECTION FIRST. I originally called this a REPRICING -- 'at genus 0 the degree condition is provably idle'. A fresh-context audit refuted that (I-1650, I-1653) and I accepted it in eb-series commit 33cb26bae1. The truth: at genus 0, for every T and every lam, the antecedent of hrig and membership in pic0Subgroup are EQUIVALENT, so hrig is hvan with the same predicate spelled '= 1' rather than 'deg = 0'. The degree left the NOTATION, not the mathematics. The tell was in my own file: the converse needs no genus hypothesis, and a genuinely weaker target does not round-trip for free.\n\nWHAT IS THEREFORE TRUE AND USEFUL:\n (a) pic0Vanishing_iff_rigidity -- hvan at EVERY test object is one hypothesis with field-point rigidity of picEt, both directions. The gain is STATABILITY: classDeg carries five fibre binders (all five measured as genuinely required, one dying at 20000 heartbeats) that do not synthesize through the relCurve def barrier, and the triviality spelling needs none of them. So hypotheses that could not be STATED at a general prime become statable.\n (b) rigidity_iff_rigidityAff -- the test-object quantifier drops: the vanishing follows from a hypothesis with NO SCHEME in it, only k-algebras, plus classes, and algebra maps into fields, and that form is NOT stronger (converse landed after the audit pointed out my caveat left it unproved). jacobianData_of_rigidityAff composes to the goal object; the P1 forms discharge the genus.\n (c) fibre_eq_one_of_mem_pic0Subgroup -- the reusable half, general in the test; pic-g's ring-level engine work consumes it.\n (d) Pic0RingDatumEngine -- at genus 0 the RE-4 rigid engine's fibrewise hypothesis is FREE (witness: the ZERO divisor, whose H1 has dimension genus C at every field extension), so H1(C_B,F)=0, H0 finite projective, H0 stalk rank 1 at every prime. pic-g's htriv_of_pic0 then removes its binder entirely.\n (e) picClass_eq_one_of_isUnit_eqn -- unit local equations present the TRIVIAL class, generic in the scheme, no curve/ring/degree/cohomology. Only producer in the tree that ESTABLISHES rather than transports triviality (verified by census, not grep). It closes the degree-0 certified chain at CechPic level, where divEq_trivEqns_of_isCertified_zero stopped at the DivFam quotient.\n\nSTILL OWED, and unowned: hrigAff has NO producer. Field-point separation is not implied by the landed separation results -- PicEtAff.unit_injective and relPicAlgMap_injective_of_etaleCover are separation along ETALE COVERS, and a field point is not one unless A is already a field (audited as correct). The cheapest refutation site for hrigAff, unchecked by anyone: A = the zero ring, where the antecedent is vacuous.\n\nTWO PRICING CORRECTIONS OTHER LANES SHOULD READ. (i) The evaluation map pi^*pi_*L -> L IS in mathlib -- the counit of Scheme.Modules.pullbackPushforwardAdjunction, applied in the sibling in two files. My earlier absolute was false and unmeasured. The defensible residue is that no theorem says the counit is an ISO at a sheaf of this kind, and AJCR's carriers are not Scheme.Modules, so reaching it is a port. (ii) The bookkeeping in Pic0RigidityAffineReduction is NOT what carries its headline (which also follows from pre-session material); what it buys is the general-T form.",
